Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Redumper GUI
Upstream-Contact: Deterous <https://github.com/Deterous>
Source: https://github.com/Deterous/Redumper-GUI
Comment: The orig tarball is upstream's tagged source with a pinned Cargo.lock
 and its dependency crates vendored into vendor/ (see
 scripts/rust-vendor-tarball.sh), because the Launchpad build farm has no
 network. The vendored crates carry their own licenses in
 vendor/<crate>/LICENSE*; they are build inputs, and the resulting binary is
 statically linked against them.

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Deterous
License: GPL-3.0-only
Comment: Upstream ships the plain GPL-3.0 text with no per-file headers and no
 license field in Cargo.toml, so nothing states "or any later version".
 Packaged as the narrower GPL-3.0-only; asking upstream to declare the license
 in Cargo.toml is part of the packaging PR.

